  "content_en": "Dahan Yanhua 1 Nightmare [Second update on New Year's Eve] She thought, she was dreaming again. The afternoon sun shines on my body, giving me a warm feeling. This dream is like countless similar dreams in the past. It is still a long stretch of pavilions and wide-angle cornices in the distance. In front of you is a long stone staircase that extends to the end of the high platform. On the high platform, there is a majestic three-story palace with vermilion lacquer columns standing ten steps apart, stretching for a total of twelve. Above it is the heavy roof of the verandah, with a straight and long main ridge, double eaves and flying corners. The whole palace is solemn and solemn, like a creeping eagle spreading its wings to fly into the sky. When people stand in front of it, they are in awe unconsciously. She picked up her skirt, passed the black armor guards holding halberds on both sides of the stone steps, and ran up the stone steps, wanting to take a look at this spectacular palace. The skirt dragged over the edge of the steps, giving it a strange dragging feeling. After running for a while, she felt a little tired, so she stopped and wiped her forehead with her hand. Suddenly, a faint cry was heard in the palace on the high platform, and the sound of a woman arguing fiercely was heard again, but because it was a little far away, it was blurry and broken. Feeling anxious, I hurried a few steps further. The speaker was suddenly replaced by the female voice who had been crying just now. She was as delicate as a willow, and the beautiful charm of pearls falling on a jade plate gradually became clearer. \"... Even if there is something wrong with me, the queen can also reprimand me, so why slap me?\" ?\" The other party sneered, \"That's not what you said when you insulted my old woman before.\" \"——Qi Yi. \"Could it be that the famous Empress Lu and Mrs. Qi in the Han Palace are entering her dream this time? As she finished speaking, she stepped onto the last stone step. So the majestic and tall double-leaf palace doors were laid out in front of them, painted in vermilion with many rows of gilt door nails. In the middle, the gilt Taotie pavilion stood tall and cool, just above her forehead. Outside the palace gate, two rows of palace maids and eunuchs, who were carrying pots, serving pots, and making sullen sounds, all looked over. A female officer with a smooth forehead on her right hand was startled when she saw her. She hurriedly stepped out and pulled her over. She put her index finger on her lips and made a silencing gesture. She took her aside and said in a very soft voice, \"My little ancestor, why are you here? All the slaves in Jiaofang Palace are dead.\" She said He smiled, not paying attention to her words, and pointed to the shadowy figure in the middle of the palace, and asked in a low voice, \"What's going on inside?\" \"It's not that bitch Qi Ji.\" The female officer gritted her teeth and said, \"The queen is already generous enough not to care about her, but she is determined to make things difficult. We bumped into each other in the wine pool today, and it's even more... The words were extremely rude. The queen was so angry that she slapped her. His Majesty came over and saw...\" Finally he sighed, \"Your Majesty is so partial to Mrs. Qi. I really don't know who the queen is in Changle Palace.\" \"Oh, it's not good for Aunt Su to say that.\" On the other side of the palace door, she pointed her chin. The female official turned her head and curled her lips with a smile, and said sarcastically, \"Queen Lu is old and beautiful, and has not been favored for a long time. If she were our wife, she would have been ashamed and left the palace. But she still insists on hating our wife. Who is right?\" She didn't pay much attention to the arguments between the two female officials, and stretched out her head to inspect the scene in the palace. In the east chamber, black curtains hang from the lintel, rolled up in sections, and hung down to form ribbons, covering the figure of the woman in the queen's dress. Lu Pheasant walked out. Although her appearance was not very beautiful, there was a strong and determined look between her brows. It was the face that had appeared in her dream. She said bitterly, \"One day, I will make sure you repay tenfold the shame you have inflicted on my mother and son.\" \"Pa— —\" Emperor Gao, who was sitting on the couch behind the case, stood up angrily when he heard this. He dropped the sapphire earcup on the case with his black sleeves, and it cracked loudly. He shouted angrily, \"Lu Zhi, don't think that because you are the queen, I can't destroy you.\" There was a moment of silence in the hall. No one inside or outside the palace dared to make a sound. On the ground were fragments of light green jade. Lu Pheasant stood among them, his expression suddenly confused for a moment. Soon, she re-armed herself, stood in front of Liu Bang and straightened her back, sneered and raised her eyebrows and said, \"If Your Majesty really wants to abandon this concubine for the sake of this little concubine, I will not dare to resign. But please remove your armor and return to your hometown, if your Majesty. In the past, people in the farmland were contented with themselves. I only lamented that I could not serve the emperor until he was old, and I only hoped that your majesty would remember the words of your concubine in the third year of Han Dynasty. \"Oh, what does the queen mean? I don't understand.\" A long voice came out from behind the curtain. The young woman in the lake green skirt had a jade-like side face, slightly red and swollen. Her cloud-like hair was pulled into a bun, and she was single.It's the figure that makes people's hearts beat, and the beauty is made in heaven. Qi Yi came up from behind Liu Bang, so beautiful and sexy. \"I don't know what your majesty promised my sister that day, but I think that promises are a favor from the giver, not a barrier from the recipient. If the queen expects to rely on a promise to be careless, she will be disrespectful of your kindness.\" \"Your majesty, what's wrong?\" She glanced sideways at Liu Bang, and the last note was soft and charming, and it was soft and gentle to her ears. Liu Bang was ecstatic, his sober and broad eyes were filled with tenderness, he took her hand and coughed, \"Yi'er is right, for the sake of your two brothers, Queen, I will forgive you this time. Please reply The Jiaofang Palace faces the wall for a month. After that, you should stay in the Jiaofang Palace and don’t go out to cause trouble.\" Qi Yi’s beautiful eyes flashed with disappointment, and Lu Zhi looked at him coldly and sneered. In the distance, the long sleeves of the three people in the east chamber are flowing. Lu Zhi stands with his back to the palace door, his hands behind his back, and the veins on them are clearly visible. Instead, her voice calmed down and she said calmly, \"Promise.\" The veins on those thick hands fell into her eyes outside the hall, and the sound was like a fire, igniting all her indignation. As if all Lu Zhi's anger could be felt in her heart for a moment, she suddenly broke away from Aunt Su's hand, dropped her frightened eyes, jumped into the hall, looked at Liu Bang coldly with her chin raised, and scolded , \"A heartless man.\" \"Ayan,\" Lu Fei was startled, glared at Somo outside the palace, bent down and hugged her, pulled her to him and shouted loudly, \"Why are you here? Your Majesty,\" She looked up at Liu Bang and begged, \"Ayan is still young, and children are not sensible. Your Majesty, please don't argue with her.\" \"-Ayan, why don't you admit your mistake to Your Majesty?\" \"I don't want to admit my mistake.\" She struggled hard and refused to change her words, thinking that this was just a dream of hers, like countless times before. Since it was in her dream, she could do whatever she wanted. There was nothing in heaven or on earth that she was afraid of. In her dream, she was the master, not some ridiculous fairy emperor. And she just wanted to point her finger at this heartless man and scold him with her indignant sincerity after covering up this volume of history for so many years. \"Is it great to be an emperor? You can be heartless, but you can't be too heartless. When your wife was taking care of the housework and having children for you, where was this woman named Qi? When your wife was living on the battlefield for you, and was frightened, where was she? When your wife gave you advice and helped you manage the country, where was she?\" She glanced at Qi Yi contemptuously and said, \" It is important for a person to be self-aware. A person who has given nothing, with a light smile and two tears, wants to take away something that others have paid all the price for. \"Why?\" \"Your Majesty,\" the sarcastic voice echoed in the hall, \"I'm sorry for your queen.\" A long line of words was completed in one go, ringing loudly in the empty hall. Still hanging slightly between the beams. Inside and outside the palace, all the palace officials and maids were frightened into silence by her shocking words. Lu Pheasant let go of his hand and forgot to grab the little child in front of him. The sorrow and anger in her heart for many years were suddenly hit by the childish words of a six-year-old child. She thought that she could be strong. Yes, as a mother and a queen, she could be strong and invulnerable to all kinds of poison. But as a wife and a woman, deep down, she was not without resentment. She may not love him, but if he fails her like this, it is not her feelings that are hurt, but a woman's dignity. \"Ayan.\" Lu Zhi let go of her and stood up. She never did anything useless. The two closest guards standing outside the palace door entered the palace, grabbed the girl's arms, and dragged her out of the palace. The girl was so frightened that she kicked and struggled with all her strength. Her young body was dragged backwards by the arms of two powerful guards as if they were searching for nothing, and was lifted out of the hall's red threshold. At the same time, the young captain wearing double armor came up the steps, knelt down on one knee outside the palace, and asked, \"The master of the State of Zhao has committed disrespect, what should be done?\" \"Your Majesty,\" Lu Fei looked directly at his emperor husband in the palace with a faint look in his eyes, \"You can't hurt Ayan anymore. You have already imprisoned her father, you can't imprison her anymore.\" \"Let me go.\" She struggled and shouted, but no one paid attention. The young captain was kneeling very close to her, and she could even feel the heat on the young man's skin transmitted through the Lingling armor. Could this not be a dream? In panic, she couldn't reach herI finally realized what mistake I had made. If this is not a dream, then where am I? She looked up blankly and realized that the guards holding her were tall. If she stood up straight, she could only reach their waists. Were the people of the Han Dynasty so tall? She thought doubtfully. No, that's not the case. It's not that they are getting taller, it's that they are getting smaller. She was horrified to discover that the soles of her feet, hidden under the long skirt, were no more than three inches in size, with delicate arches, exquisite and cute, but she felt like she was seeing a nightmare. What's going on? Her figure has also shrunk by half, like a girl who has not grown up. Her hair is long, and after combing it into a bun, it hangs down to her waist as before. She is wearing a peach-patterned undershirt with a crouching collar and a right hem, and a purple dress underneath. The dress is long and falls to the floor. It is a typical early Han Dynasty woman's attire, with luxurious materials and wide sleeves like clouds. In the palace, Liu Bang shifted his strange eyes from his married wife to his granddaughter, and suddenly he smiled instead of angry. Amidst the sound of footsteps, she raised her head and saw the lazy but energetic face of the elderly emperor walking towards her, \"Zhang Yan, do you know you are wrong?\" There was a lump of air in her throat, she gritted her teeth and shook her head, glaring at him stubbornly. \"Okay.\" Liu Bang raised his thumb and said with a big smile, \"This is indeed my grandson.\" His face suddenly darkened, \"Let her kneel outside the palace and get up again when she admits her mistake.\" Many years later, recalling that earth-shattering afternoon in Changle Palace in winter, it seemed like a nightmare. And Zhang Yan could only smile faintly and sigh, \"I remember when I was young.\" In fact, thinking about it afterwards, there were too many signs telling her that it was by no means a simple dream, such as the lingering fatigue when climbing the stairs, such as the long skirt dragging The feeling of falling across the stone steps is like Aunt Somo respectfully calling her Wengzhu, like Lu Pheasant calling her nickname \"Ayan\". In the past, when she dreamed, she only saw a series of silent and meandering pantomimes. When someone spoke, the dream came to an end. But that day, she actually heard every word everyone said. However, the authorities at that time were as confused as sleepwalking, relying on their own instincts to act, ignoring all obvious or hidden traces. Cultural tips of the Han Dynasty: Changle Palace is one of the two most important palaces in the Western Han Dynasty. It is located in the southeast of Chang'an City. There is a palace gate on each side of the palace city, and there are gates on the west and north. It was the political center of Gao Emperor Liu Bang's dynasty, and the palace where the queen mothers of the Western Han dynasties lived after Gao Emperor. The Chinese palace system consists of living in the front and sleeping in the back. The front hall of Changle is where the imperial court is located, and the west is the harem. The queen's palace is on the north side of the front hall. The front hall is the main building of Changle Palace. It is surrounded by walls. The gate of the palace is facing to the south and there is a courtyard inside the gate. The courtyard is vast and is where court meetings are held. The east and west chambers of the same size are symmetrically distributed on both sides of the main hall of the front hall. The east and west chambers have important purposes, among which the east chamber is more prominent. Although the emperor met with officials in the main hall, many military and government affairs were conducted in the east chamber. Ministers of civil and military affairs often wait in the east chamber before entering the main hall. What Zhang Yan broke into was the Changle front hall. It originally fell in front of the steps in the courtyard of the front hall, and the dispute between Empress Lu and Qi Yi took place in the east chamber. The first three chapters are very substantial, I hope. I wish you good luck and all the best in the Year of the Ox. Collection, recommended.",
